            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "It looks good to me"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "This looks good to me. Want to see some code underneath it before this goes."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Overall I'm fine with staging.  I must've had a misunderstanding about the design if this option will exist forever"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "You didn't misunderstand. Initially the option is needed for staging in the changes as a proving ground. Once proven I was thinking distributions would need the option for enabling/disabling the option. (Similar to redfish-aggregation.)\n\nThe lack of D-Bus objects implementing the `xyz.openbmc_project.State.BMC.Redundancy` interface would indicate there is no redundancy on the BMC. By disabling the option for a particular distribution it would save a mapper call at runtime.\n\nIs the ability to disable the option long-term not desirable? If so I will update the description of the option."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm marking this comment resolved so the bot shows reviewer as next action. Please reopen the comment if you disagree with my response."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "DBus interfaces are detectable for just about any change, so we generally don't include options for it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the explanation. I've removed the statement about this compile option staying around long-term."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 454,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "?  Once this is completed, why does this option need to exist at all?  Can't we just get the information from dbus like we do everything else?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 454,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "(Same answer and question for this review comment as for the overall review comment.)\n\nOnce proven I was thinking distributions would need the option for enabling/disabling the option. (Similar to redfish-aggregation.)\n\nThe lack of D-Bus objects implementing the xyz.openbmc_project.State.BMC.Redundancy interface indicates there is no redundancy on the BMC. By disabling the option for a particular distribution it would save a single GetSubTree mapper call at runtime. (See getManagerRedundancy())\n\nIs the ability to disable the option long-term not desirable? If so I will update the description of the option."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 454,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm marking this comment resolved so the bot shows reviewer as next action. Please reopen the comment if you disagree with my response."
                }
